claims.claim:
#11 §11.2, from the literature:
- a magnetic counterpart for every electric particle is Montonen-Olive duality, exact in maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills;
- 'magnetic quarks' is Seiberg-duality vocabulary;
- the dual superconductor is the leading confinement mechanism;
- Dirac's condition makes the magnetic world our strong-coupling mirror.
Flag 28 (confirmed, unruled): the 34 is right, but the formula beside it, 4π/e², is the 137 one.

#11 §11.3:
- the DSZ pairing makes the charge lattice a symplectic space;
- mutual locality is a Lagrangian sublattice;
- choosing a duality frame (electric = fundamental, magnetic = solitonic) is choosing a Lagrangian polarization of charge space;
- S-duality τ_c → −1/τ_c uses the same [[0,1],[−1,0]] matrix as Born's ρ and Z → −Z⁻¹, 'the third appearance of one matrix in this program'.

#14 v2 §2, 'Conjecture (the identification)':
- reciprocity acts on gauge couplings as the modular S transformation, fixing the dual sector's coupling at α_d = 1/(4α) ≈ 34;
- it does NOT assert magnetic charge under our photon; 'magnetic' means the sector's duality-frame character;
- it is called load-bearing: without it α_d becomes a free parameter.
HANDOFF.md:32 lists 'α_d ≈ 34 via Dirac quantization against our photon' as dead (round 1), restated in v2 as reciprocity-as-S.

